# Obsidian AI Agent Plugin Direct Google Cloud Vertex AI Integration

Architecture pattern for connecting Obsidian desktop plugins (e.g. `ai-agent`) directly to Google Cloud Vertex AI with automatic token refresh, zero background daemons, and multi-model Gemini selection.

## 1. Authentication Architecture (Zero Background Daemons)

Instead of running an external local proxy daemon (like Python or Node on port 8765/5199), desktop plugins running in Electron/Node can manage token lifecycle directly:

1. **Primary Auth Path: ADC Refresh Token Exchange (Fastest, ~200ms)**
   - Read `~/.config/gcloud/application_default_credentials.json`.
   - If present with `client_id`, `client_secret`, and `refresh_token`:
   - POST to `https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token`:
     ```json
     {
       "client_id": "<client_id>",
       "client_secret": "<client_secret>",
       "refresh_token": "<refresh_token>",
       "grant_type": "refresh_token"
     }
     ```
   - Returns `{ "access_token": "ya29...", "expires_in": 3599 }`.
   - Cache token in-memory and refresh automatically when expiration is within 5 minutes or on HTTP 401.

2. **Secondary Auth Path: Direct `gcloud` Execution with Path Probing**
   - In Electron desktop environments (macOS Finder launch), `process.env.PATH` is often minimal (`/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin`).
   - Probe candidate paths:
     - `/opt/homebrew/bin/gcloud` (Apple Silicon)
     - `/usr/local/bin/gcloud` (Intel macOS)
     - `~/google-cloud-sdk/bin/gcloud`
   - Execute `gcloud auth print-access-token`.

3. **Fallback: Service Account JSON Key**
   - Allow user to paste a service account JSON file.
   - Mint JWT signed with RS256 and exchange at `https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token`.

## 2. Vertex AI Endpoint & Payload Normalization Rules

### Endpoint Construction
```text
https://aiplatform.googleapis.com/v1beta1/projects/{projectId}/locations/{location}/publishers/google/models/{model}:{action}
```
- For standard generation: `:generateContent`
- For streaming: `:streamGenerateContent?alt=sse`
- Location: `locations/global` is mandatory for Gemini 3.8 (`gemini-3.8-flash`) and Gemini 4 (`gemini-4-argon`). Calling regional endpoints like `us-central1` returns HTTP 404.

### Headers
```http
Authorization: Bearer <ACCESS_TOKEN>
Content-Type: application/json
```
*(CRITICAL: Do NOT send `x-goog-api-key` to `aiplatform.googleapis.com` when Bearer token is present, as it triggers HTTP 401).*

### Critical Payload Normalization Quirks

1. **Gemini 3/4 Thought Signatures & Historical Function Calls (HTTP 400)**:
   - **Errors**:
     - `[400] Please ensure that either all function calls have responses or thought signature is provided with each function call in function call turn.`
     - `[400] Invalid thought signature.`
   - **Root Cause**:
     - Gemini 2.5/3/3.8/4 models with thinking enabled return cryptographic `thoughtSignature`s alongside tool calls.
     - Third-party plugins sometimes hardcode fake dummy signatures (e.g. `YSt = "ErYCCrMCAdHtim9k..."`), which Google's Vertex AI cryptographically validates and rejects with `Invalid thought signature`.
     - In multi-turn chat history, re-sending previous tool calls without valid cryptographic signatures or without perfectly matched responses triggers `HTTP 400`.
   - **Solution — Safe History Flattening**:
     - Do NOT inject fake signatures.
     - Before sending `parsedBody.contents` to Vertex AI, inspect all historical turns.
     - Any completed `functionCall` that lacks an active valid cryptographic signature (length < 50 or matching dummy strings) is flattened into conversational text:
       `{ text: "[Дія: tool_name(args)]" }`
     - Any completed `functionResponse` is flattened into conversational text:
       `{ text: "[Результат дії tool_name: response]" }`
     - Roles with `"function"` are mapped to `"user"`.
     - Consecutive text blocks are merged.
     - This gives the model 100% of the historical context while completely avoiding the Google Thought Signature verification failure.

```javascript
if (Array.isArray(parsedBody.contents)) {
  let origContents = parsedBody.contents;
  let newContents = [];
  for (let cIdx = 0; cIdx < origContents.length; cIdx++) {
    let turn = origContents[cIdx];
    if (!turn) continue;
    let role = turn.role || "user";
    let parts = Array.isArray(turn.parts) ? turn.parts : [];
    let newParts = [];

    for (let p of parts) {
      if (p && p.functionCall) {
        let fc = p.functionCall;
        let sig = p.thoughtSignature;
        if (!sig || sig.includes("ErYCCrMCAdHtim9k") || sig.length < 50) {
          let argsStr = "";
          try { argsStr = JSON.stringify(fc.args || {}); } catch(_) {}
          newParts.push({ text: `[Дія: ${fc.name || "tool"}(${argsStr})]` });
        } else {
          newParts.push(p);
        }
      } else if (p && p.functionResponse) {
        let fr = p.functionResponse;
        let respStr = "";
        try {
          respStr = typeof fr.response === "string" ? fr.response : JSON.stringify(fr.response || {});
        } catch(_) {}
        newParts.push({ text: `[Результат дії ${fr.name || "інструменту"}: ${respStr}]` });
      } else {
        newParts.push(p);
      }
    }

    // Merge consecutive text parts
    let mergedParts = [];
    for (let np of newParts) {
      if (np.text && mergedParts.length > 0 && mergedParts[mergedParts.length - 1].text) {
        mergedParts[mergedParts.length - 1].text += "\n" + np.text;
      } else {
        mergedParts.push(np);
      }
    }

    if (role === "function") role = "user";
    newContents.push({ role, parts: mergedParts.length > 0 ? mergedParts : [{ text: "..." }] });
  }
  parsedBody.contents = newContents;
}
```

2. **Thinking Config Compatibility**:
   - `gemini-2.5-flash` and `gemini-2.5-pro` reject `thinkingConfig.thinkingLevel`. Sending `thinkingLevel: "low"|"high"` results in:
     `HTTP 400 Unable to submit request because thinking_level is not supported by this model`.
   - `thinkingLevel` is only supported on Gemini 3.x series (`gemini-3.7-flash`, `gemini-3.8-flash`). Strip `thinkingLevel` when targeting non-3.x models.

3. **Suggested Models List**:
   - `gemini-3.8-flash`: SOTA Fast & Intelligent, default for agentic chat and UI extensions.
   - `gemini-4-argon`: Next-Gen flagship reasoning model.
   - `gemini-2.5-flash`: Fast fallback.
   - `gemini-2.5-pro`: Deep reasoning & coding.
